CloudBurrow patch 16 to github.com/goccy/bigquery-emulator v0.8.1
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#1369). Needs patches 0002 and 0009 and
googlesqlite patch 0019.

The bug: jobs.list (Project.Jobs, findProjectJobs) read the project's
jobs with a GoogleSQL `id IN UNNEST(@jobIDs)`, which googlesqlite
compiles to a function call per row and element, so a list cost more
with every job: 8.7 s for 5,000 jobs (measured through CloudBurrow's
front, 2026-10-15, arm64 kind node). INFORMATION_SCHEMA.JOBS reads the
list, and passed a minute after about 3,000 jobs.

The patch reads the project's rows of the jobs table with one SQLite
scan (googlesqlite's Conn.QueryRawContext, as patch 0009 reads one job),
decodes them as googlesqlite would, and lists them in the order
cloudburrow_job_order keeps, as before.

